    "direction": "2026-10-09 Amir picked 2c: small black 12-inch record centred, art circle = 90% of the record (thin black rim), title + name under it. Mood M4 used in sketches, not confirmed. Art inside the circle not chosen yet. Sketch: artwork/edits/misty-night-direction-2c-sketch.jpg. | 2026-10-13 Amir: cover direction = \"D2\" sketch (round 6, artwork/edits/half-the-night-sketch-round6.jpg) for direction only: warm grey paper, embossed circle with record grooves, his silhouette (out-073) on one horizontal axis with a dithered reflection below, hawk-like ravens crossing from the reflection over his legs and out top right (dithered below the line, solid above), \"inch of shadow\" on the axis, title in wide-spaced serif caps (font not final), small technical text in the corners. Reference: A Perfect Circle \"To Whom It May Concern\". Ravens to be replaced by real ones later (own photos). | 2026-10-14 Amir: elements go AI (inked), composited locally on the D2 layout, no text, no playground filters (he adjusts in the playground later). Picks: ravens = AI final sheet B plus 3 birds from sheet A; swan = black swan B, Amir picked the BLACK swan (B) 2026-10-14; the violet swan is set aside. Out: sun, moon, hourglass, cricket. Exports: artwork/edits/half-the-night-r14-swan-black.png, -swan-violet1.png, -swan-violet2.png (1080 px; r13 had a wrong raven over him, fixed in r14: every bird keeps its draft position and direction, A birds only away from him). AI records: generated_images/imagine/pinocchio-single_20261014-0342*/0343*/0344*.json.",
